The MS format uses the bitshift-trellis construction and the 1MAD decoding function described in QTIP
(A. Tseng, Q. Sun, D. Hou, C. De Sa, "QTIP: Quantization with Trellises and Incoherence Processing", NeurIPS 2024,
arXiv:2406.11235). This software contains no code from QTIP or QuIP#.

The per-tensor bit allocation of the Qwen3.8-27B tiers starts from the per-tensor quantization types of unsloth's
Unsloth Dynamic GGUFs (https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF, Apache License 2.0), and the converter copies the
tensors MS does not code (the input token table, norms and small SSM tensors) from those files into the Qwen3.8-27B MS files.

madshift/gdn.py is derived from Hugging Face transformers (src/transformers/models/qwen3_5/modeling_qwen3_5.py),
Copyright 2025 The Qwen Team and The HuggingFace Inc. team, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The converter reads and writes GGUF files with gguf-py from llama.cpp (MIT License, Copyright the ggml authors), as included
in the MS llama.cpp fork (https://github.com/devvexus/ms-llama.cpp); gguf-py is a dependency and is not included here.
